1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,585
- [OLIVER]<i> Pa.</i>
<i>- Hm?</i>

2
00:00:02,669 --> 00:00:03,837
<i>Time to take your medicine.</i>

3
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,714
<i>What about you? Did you take yours?</i>

4
00:00:05,797 --> 00:00:08,550
<i>- Got mine ready. Here.</i>
<i>- Okay. Together, then?</i>

5
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:10,093
<i>- Cheers.</i>
<i>- Hm.</i>

6
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:16,141
<i>There, all done.</i>

7
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:18,893
<i>- Dad? Um…</i>
<i>- Hmm?</i>

8
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:22,439
<i>You have a follow-up consultation</i>
<i>with the doctor tomorrow.</i>

9
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:23,815
<i>That's right.</i>

10
00:00:24,482 --> 00:00:28,528
<i>Don't force yourself</i>
<i>to go back to work too soon.</i>

11
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:31,031
<i>I feel like I'll be fine by next week.</i>

12
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:34,242
<i>Sweetheart, there's something</i>
<i>I need to tell you.</i>

13
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:36,536
<i>What is it?</i>

14
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:40,123
<i>I want to go visit</i>
<i>Bea and Mariela for a bit.</i>

15
00:00:40,206 --> 00:00:41,541
[JORDAN] <i>Dude, come on.</i>

16
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:45,462
<i>I know that</i>
<i>your hospital bills are piling up.</i>

17
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:47,255
<i>Please, let me help.</i>

18
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:49,424
<i>Just a little.</i>

19
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:53,511
<i>Dude, it's me, okay?</i>

20
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:56,139
<i>Remember me, Jordan, your best friend?</i>

21
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,933
Of course we got each other's backs.

22
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:02,479
<i>What about you? How's your dad?</i>

23
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:04,397
<i>He's doing okay.</i>

24
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,608
<i>What about Bea?</i>

25
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:09,819
<i>I still can't believe that</i>
<i>she's my sister.</i>

26
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:13,782
<i>Well, at least your question</i>
<i>has been answered.</i>

27
00:01:14,991 --> 00:01:17,077
<i>We finally know why Bea is mad at you.</i>

28
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,370
<i>Why she did everything</i>
<i>that she did to you,</i>

29
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:22,832
<i>to LoveList, and to your family.</i>

30
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,626
<i>Because she was hurt?</i>

31
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:30,256
<i>Can you forgive her?</i>

32
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:37,597
[PRISON GUARD]
<i>Mercado, you two have visitors.</i>

33
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:40,141
<i>We have visitors? Who are they?</i>

34
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:43,186
[PRISON GUARD]
<i>Benilda Cariño and Enrico Dominguez.</i>

35
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:45,104
[BEA] <i>I need you to do something.</i>

36
00:01:47,023 --> 00:01:49,359
<i>Ma! Ma! Ma! Ma!</i>

37
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:52,362
<i>I already erased you from my life!</i>

38
00:01:52,445 --> 00:01:54,697
<i>- Dad, let's go.</i>
<i>- It's all your fault, Enrico!</i>

39
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:56,282
<i>Stay out of this!</i>

40
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:58,159
<i>You're just his mistress's daughter!</i>

41
00:01:58,743 --> 00:02:00,578
[BEA] <i>Ma, don't get mad at Billy.</i>

42
00:02:00,662 --> 00:02:03,039
<i>Billy didn't take anything from us.</i>
<i>She has nothing to do with all this.</i>

43
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:06,626
<i>We shouldn't have taken out</i>
<i>our anger on her.</i>

44
00:02:06,709 --> 00:02:08,545
[BILLY] <i>Let's regroup tomorrow morning.</i>

45
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:10,421
<i>But, Billy, tomorrow…</i>

46
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:11,798
<i>tomorrow is Saturday.</i>

47
00:02:11,881 --> 00:02:14,300
<i>Yani and I have plans.</i>

48
00:02:15,343 --> 00:02:16,928
<i>I know it's the weekend.</i>

49
00:02:18,805 --> 00:02:19,639
<i>Guys.</i>

50
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:24,602
<i>The company is</i>
<i>literally bleeding right now.</i>

51
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:26,437
<i>Where's your commitment to your work?</i>

52
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:31,442
[JORDAN] <i>Maybe we can do a Zoom meeting?</i>

53
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:35,029
<i>- Guys, how's your Saturday?</i>
- [BLAIRE] <i>I'm free.</i>

54
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:36,531
<i>- Okay.</i>
<i>- No, it's fine.</i>

55
00:02:36,614 --> 00:02:38,575
<i>- Sunday?</i>
<i>- No. I'll see you Monday.</i>

56
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:39,742
[JORDAN] <i>Billy?</i>

57
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:56,384
[EXHALES SLOWLY]

58
00:02:57,719 --> 00:03:03,683
["TABLA TAYO" BY FANA PLAYING]

59
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:06,686
[LOUD BANG]

60
00:03:30,043 --> 00:03:31,377
I heard that.

61
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:38,927
Dude, I know this isn't
just about the company.

62
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:41,304
It is about the company.

63
00:03:43,139 --> 00:03:45,183
We're not in a good place right now.

64
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:48,353
Or maybe

65
00:03:49,103 --> 00:03:51,147
it's about what your Dad wants.

66
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:53,900
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

67
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:56,653
Can you give him what he wants?

68
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:01,658
[SOFT THUD]

69
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:07,580
I don't know.

70
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:15,380
Maybe you just need a break.

71
00:04:19,217 --> 00:04:20,551
Come to my gig tonight.

72
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:26,349
- Gig?
- Yes. It will be fun.

73
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:32,105
With everything on my plate right now,

74
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:33,815
you want me to come to your gig?

75
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:37,986
No, thank you.

76
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:43,741
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

77
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:54,752
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:05:56,397 --> 00:05:58,232
Take this phone. You can have it.

79
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:02,570
But that gun you're holding,
I'll sell that to you for forty.

80
00:06:02,653 --> 00:06:04,655
- Magazine included.
- Forty?

81
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:07,158
- [COCKS GUN]
- You sure about that?

82
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:08,326
Hm?

83
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:09,744
That's already at cost.

84
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:11,204
Is this really how you'll treat me?

85
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:14,040
When your shop was raided
for forging documents,

86
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:15,833
who helped you?

87
00:06:16,417 --> 00:06:19,337
Me, remember?
I cleaned all your computers.

88
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,839
You'd be behind bars now
if it weren't for me.

89
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:23,925
- Forget it.
- No, I'll pay.

90
00:06:24,008 --> 00:06:25,635
I don't want to get dragged
into your mess.

91
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:27,303
I've got you.

92
00:06:27,386 --> 00:06:31,557
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:35,228
I'll just get back at them
for what they've done.

94
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:41,067
They didn't spare my girlfriend's mom,
so I'll make these bastards pay.

95
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:42,568
- You copy?
- G-Got it, bro.

96
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:44,904
Just pay me when you can.

97
00:06:44,987 --> 00:06:45,947
Put that away.

98
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:49,659
How about your companion?
Does he have money?

99
00:06:49,742 --> 00:06:50,827
Where is he?

100
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:52,787
Beats me.

101
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,790
Hey, everyone!

102
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:57,083
We're live again,

103
00:06:57,166 --> 00:07:01,796
and I've got so much in store
for you guys!

104
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:03,381
We've got perfumes.

105
00:07:03,464 --> 00:07:05,508
We've got makeup.

106
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:08,094
And we've got anti-aging products too!

107
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:11,431
So, please stay tuned
and share our livestream.

108
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:14,559
Here are the new scents from Halimuyak!

109
00:07:14,642 --> 00:07:18,479
Perfect for mornings, evenings--

110
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:20,898
You can wear it all day!

111
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:22,567
You've been requesting these, right?

112
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:24,819
- See? I listen to your--
- [KNOCKS ON DOOR]

113
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:31,784
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:07:34,412 --> 00:07:35,413
Did you miss me?

115
00:07:35,496 --> 00:07:40,751
[TENSE MUSIC SWELLS]

116
00:07:40,835 --> 00:07:42,128
[MUSIC STOPS]

117
00:07:43,337 --> 00:07:45,381
[DINO] Are you still upset with me?

118
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:49,385
I kept my promise. I returned to you.

119
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:50,428
[KAREN SCOFFS]

120
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:53,055
Yeah, you did keep your promise.

121
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:56,601
But coming back as a fugitive
wasn't part of the deal.

122
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:59,604
What's your plan now? Go into hiding?

123
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,773
I had someone make
a fake ID and passport for me.

124
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:05,526
Passport? Oh, wow!

125
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:06,777
You're going abroad?

126
00:08:06,861 --> 00:08:08,988
You should take me with you.
What's your destination?

127
00:08:09,071 --> 00:08:11,324
US? Europe?

128
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:13,075
How about Africa?

129
00:08:13,159 --> 00:08:15,119
[KAREN LAUGHS]

130
00:08:15,203 --> 00:08:18,414
I just need a new name and a new identity.

131
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:22,293
Oh! You're gonna turn over a new leaf?

132
00:08:23,252 --> 00:08:26,797
You won't be doing you-know-what anymore

133
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:28,424
and get a proper job?

134
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:32,011
If I manage to, why not?

135
00:08:32,094 --> 00:08:33,679
But before that,

136
00:08:33,763 --> 00:08:36,599
I'll make some old clients pay their dues.

137
00:08:36,682 --> 00:08:39,769
You think they'll pay? I doubt it.

138
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:41,312
They might just report you.

139
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:43,523
Let's see them try.

140
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:47,109
Fine.

141
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,487
I'll just buy some ice.

142
00:08:51,113 --> 00:08:56,369
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

143
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:05,211
- [POLICE SIREN BLARES]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

144
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:23,271
[KAREN] <i>Why did you follow me?</i>

145
00:09:25,314 --> 00:09:27,692
- I thought you'd--
- Report you?

146
00:09:28,401 --> 00:09:31,487
If I wanted to,
I would have done it when I found out--

147
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:33,155
I was selling drugs?

148
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:37,535
Yeah. I don't know which hurt more.

149
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:41,414
Finding out you were a drug dealer

150
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:43,791
or learning you were married.

151
00:09:43,874 --> 00:09:45,793
[GROUP SINGING]
<i>♪ …wherever it takes me ♪</i>

152
00:09:45,876 --> 00:09:49,463
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

153
00:09:49,547 --> 00:09:50,756
Whose song is this?

154
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,509
<i>- ♪ Wherever I go ♪</i>
- Why do you ask?

155
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:57,555
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

156
00:09:57,638 --> 00:10:01,517
<i>♪ Even if you let go</i>
<i>I'll come back ♪</i>

157
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:06,063
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

158
00:10:06,147 --> 00:10:09,191
<i>♪ Wherever I go ♪</i>

159
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:13,279
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

160
00:10:13,362 --> 00:10:14,947
<i>♪ Even if you let go ♪</i>

161
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:17,658
<i>♪ I'll come back ♪</i>

162
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:21,495
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

163
00:10:21,579 --> 00:10:22,997
You know that boy?

164
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:28,294
<i>♪ Stay right there, my love</i>
<i>Because I'm coming home ♪</i>

165
00:10:28,377 --> 00:10:29,629
He's my son.

166
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:31,881
And this song?

167
00:10:32,673 --> 00:10:35,635
His mother wrote it for Jordan and me.

168
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:38,554
- Jade wrote that?
<i>- ♪ I'm already weak and wounded ♪</i>

169
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:42,433
<i>♪ It seems I'm drowning in sorrow… ♪</i>

170
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:46,896
[JADE, YOUNG JORDAN SINGING]
<i>♪ I'll ride your wave ♪</i>

171
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:51,067
<i>♪ Wherever it takes me ♪</i>

172
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:56,489
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

173
00:10:56,572 --> 00:10:59,533
<i>♪ Wherever I go ♪</i>

174
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:03,579
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

175
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:07,667
<i>♪ Even if you let go, I'll come back ♪</i>

176
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:12,713
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

177
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:18,719
<i>♪ Stay right there, my love</i>
<i>Because I'm coming home ♪</i>

178
00:11:19,303 --> 00:11:20,388
[JADE CHUCKLES]

179
00:11:22,515 --> 00:11:23,724
Really?

180
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:27,144
- That Jordan is your son? Him?
<i>- </i>[JORDAN KEEPS SINGING IN VIDEO]

181
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:30,940
Don't you see? It says "Jordan Valentin."

182
00:11:31,023 --> 00:11:32,358
His surname is Valentin.

183
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:37,947
[VIDEO KEEPS PLAYING]

184
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:43,285
<i>So, finally, our fangirling era</i>
<i>has brought us</i>

185
00:11:43,369 --> 00:11:45,246
<i>here to Jade & Jude's!</i>

186
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:47,373
<i>Whoo! My heart!</i>

187
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:49,792
<i>Jordan, I can't wait</i>
<i>to see you perform live!</i>

188
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:50,918
<i>I love you!</i>

189
00:11:51,001 --> 00:11:52,586
<i>Whoo!</i>

190
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:56,048
Nice! Your son is a big shot.

191
00:11:56,132 --> 00:11:59,927
Wow! How cool!

192
00:12:00,010 --> 00:12:06,016
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

193
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:10,479
Ma.

194
00:12:11,522 --> 00:12:13,107
It won't be long

195
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:15,651
before we finally get out of here.

196
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:20,281
Just a few more nudges
and that Billy will give in.

197
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:24,535
If she continues to feel sorry for me,

198
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:29,081
she'll drop the charges against me.

199
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:31,584
And then she'll have
your case dismissed too.

200
00:12:33,085 --> 00:12:34,086
So, Ma,

201
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,714
here's the plan.

202
00:12:36,797 --> 00:12:38,507
The next time they visit us,

203
00:12:39,258 --> 00:12:41,510
we'll put on an act again.

204
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:44,180
You'll pretend to feel sorry

205
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:46,932
and apologize to them, okay?

206
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:48,225
You know what?

207
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:54,273
I can feel that your father
is genuinely sorry.

208
00:12:55,524 --> 00:12:58,194
Do you think

209
00:12:59,069 --> 00:13:00,404
he still loves me?

210
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:03,657
Um…

211
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:06,118
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:08,996
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
That's possible, Ma.

213
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,707
I was thinking the same thing.

214
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:12,875
It's possible.

215
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:16,003
But there's a problem.

216
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:19,673
That Billy and her aunt.

217
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:21,967
I hate sharing.

218
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:23,802
No way.

219
00:13:24,553 --> 00:13:26,305
We are the first family,

220
00:13:26,388 --> 00:13:29,767
so your father is ours alone.

221
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,809
Do you understand?

222
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:36,815
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

223
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:44,573
It's 140 over 90.

224
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:47,535
Your blood pressure is high, Enrico.
You need to take your meds.

225
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:48,786
Here.

226
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:50,871
Oh. Be careful.

227
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:54,041
Enrico, please take care of yourself.

228
00:13:54,124 --> 00:13:55,793
Avoid any stress, okay?

229
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:58,587
[SIGHS] Mariela still hasn't changed.

230
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:01,590
Even when we were still together,

231
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:05,135
she'd throw a fit and hurt others
when she was upset.

232
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:08,430
[SIGHS] There's nothing you
can do to help her.

233
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,558
What do you want?

234
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:13,894
Do you want Billy to forgive Mariela too?

235
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:16,689
[ENRICO] No.

236
00:14:16,772 --> 00:14:18,274
No.

237
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:21,694
I'm sorry. Go take your medicine.

238
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:25,197
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

239
00:14:25,281 --> 00:14:26,699
Hmm.

240
00:14:26,782 --> 00:14:30,870
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

241
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:33,539
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

242
00:14:33,622 --> 00:14:35,249
[WOMEN SQUEALING]

243
00:14:35,332 --> 00:14:37,459
[WOMAN] How much longer
do we have to wait?

244
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:39,920
We've been here for almost
an hour already.

245
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:41,547
- Oh, yeah--
- Right, guys?

246
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:43,299
[CROWD] Yeah!

247
00:14:43,382 --> 00:14:44,425
[ROBBIE] Yeah. Yeah, I know.

248
00:14:44,508 --> 00:14:46,427
We'll open soon.

249
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:48,387
We don't open until six.

250
00:14:48,470 --> 00:14:49,889
You know that, right?

251
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:51,390
- Open it now.
- Let us inside.

252
00:14:51,473 --> 00:14:55,102
Please be patient.
We'll give free chicken wings later.

253
00:14:55,185 --> 00:14:57,271
But is it okay if they're no longer hot?

254
00:14:57,354 --> 00:15:00,357
- We want to go inside.
- Please, guys. Be patient.

255
00:15:00,441 --> 00:15:01,859
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

256
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:03,444
[RAIN] Okay. Announcement.

257
00:15:03,527 --> 00:15:06,030
- We'll open in three minutes.
- [CROWD] Whoo!

258
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:08,073
- [RAIN] Three minutes, okay?
- Yay!

259
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:09,241
- How exciting!
- Whoo!

260
00:15:09,325 --> 00:15:12,328
- Please fall in line.
- [WOMAN] Gosh, I'll see Jordan!

261
00:15:12,411 --> 00:15:17,041
[ROBBIE] I know that you're all excited,
but please fall in line.

262
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:19,043
- [ROBBIE] There. At the back.
- Oh, look.

263
00:15:19,126 --> 00:15:22,338
- [RAIN] It's Marj. Excuse me.
- [ROBBIE] Make way, please.

264
00:15:22,421 --> 00:15:23,589
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:26,300
- [WOMAN] Who are they?
- Hi, ma'am.

266
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:31,180
Hey, why did you let them inside?

267
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:32,681
You told us to wait in line.

268
00:15:32,765 --> 00:15:36,560
We've been waiting here for ages,
and you just let them cut in line?

269
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:37,728
- She's right.
- Right?

270
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:40,022
- [RAIN] Ma'am, please wait.
- Look at the time!

271
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,982
- That's unfair!
- [ROBBIE] Ma'am, ma'am.

272
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:45,152
Calm down, okay?
We'll open in a few minutes.

273
00:15:45,235 --> 00:15:46,737
- That's unfair!
- We were waiting here.

274
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:49,490
[ROBBIE] We'll open soon. I promise.

275
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:52,618
It'll just be a few minutes.
You'll get inside soon.

276
00:15:52,701 --> 00:15:59,708
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

277
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:13,138
- [WOMAN 1] Hurry! We're late!
- [WOMAN 2] I know. All right.

278
00:16:14,348 --> 00:16:17,977
- [WOMAN 3] We'll see Jordan.
- [WOMAN 4] Oh my gosh! Come on!

279
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:24,984
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

280
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:43,085
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

281
00:16:43,168 --> 00:16:46,505
[INDISTINCT EXCITED CHATTER]

282
00:16:53,345 --> 00:16:54,847
- [WOMAN] Come on!
- [MAN] Let us in!

283
00:16:54,930 --> 00:16:57,391
- We'll open soon.
- Just wait, please.

284
00:16:57,474 --> 00:16:59,852
- That's a promise.
- We want to go inside now.

285
00:16:59,935 --> 00:17:06,400
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

286
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:19,830
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

287
00:17:19,913 --> 00:17:21,498
This is taking so long.

288
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:23,667
- [RAIN] You can go inside now.
- [ROBBIE] Come in.

289
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:25,627
[RAIN] One by one, please.

290
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:28,130
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

291
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:30,007
[RAIN] Again, one by one, please.

292
00:17:33,093 --> 00:17:34,553
[RAIN] Watch your step.

293
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:39,308
- [MAN] Finally, we're going in.
- [WOMAN] This is great!

294
00:17:39,391 --> 00:17:46,148
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

295
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:57,868
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

296
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:12,132
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

297
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:14,051
<i>- Come here!</i>
<i>- Hey!</i>

298
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:16,512
<i>- Caloy!</i>
<i>- What were you doing there?</i>

299
00:18:16,595 --> 00:18:17,930
<i>And why are you meddling, huh?</i>

300
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:19,389
<i>Who was your target there?</i>

301
00:18:21,391 --> 00:18:22,309
<i>Jordan.</i>

302
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:23,519
<i>Jordan Valentin?</i>

303
00:18:23,602 --> 00:18:25,145
[VALERIE] <i>Oh my gosh!</i>

304
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:28,440
<i>Your live performance video</i>
<i>has reached 100,000 views.</i>

305
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:31,318
<i>- Really?</i>
<i>- And my wall is flooded with inquiries.</i>

306
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:32,569
<i>Great.</i>

307
00:18:32,653 --> 00:18:34,530
<i>You seemed distracted earlier.</i>

308
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:37,241
<i>Is it because of Billy again?</i>

309
00:18:39,535 --> 00:18:42,162
<i>- Did you invite her?</i>
<i>- Yes, of course.</i>

310
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:44,206
<i>Did you really expect her to come</i>

311
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:47,084
<i>after losing her cool</i>
<i>at the office earlier?</i>

312
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:49,419
<i>She already said no.</i>

313
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:53,674
<i>But I was still hoping</i>
<i>she'd change her mind.</i>

314
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:55,342
<i>That jerk did me wrong.</i>

315
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:58,720
<i>- He did you wrong?</i>
<i>- Yes. And the woman I love.</i>

316
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:01,473
<i>They filed several charges</i>
<i>against us and sent me to jail.</i>

317
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:03,892
<i>That's why I want to get back at him.</i>

318
00:19:04,476 --> 00:19:06,562
<i>Don't you dare hurt Jordan.</i>

319
00:19:06,645 --> 00:19:10,566
<i>If it weren't for me,</i>
<i>you'd still be in jail.</i>

320
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:12,151
<i>Is that clear?</i>

321
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:15,571
<i>We'll get out of here, Ma.</i>

322
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:19,032
<i>We'll rise up from this.</i>

323
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:21,952
<i>And if you still love Papa,</i>

324
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:25,330
<i>I'll take him back for you.</i>

325
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:28,167
<i>Our family will be complete again.</i>

326
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:35,257
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

327
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:39,595
[JORDAN SINGING IN VIDEO]
<i>♪ My muse ♪</i>

328
00:19:39,678 --> 00:19:43,307
<i>- ♪ Where's our destination? ♪</i>
- [CROWD CHEERING]

329
00:19:44,808 --> 00:19:47,311
<i>♪ You are the captain ♪</i>

330
00:19:47,394 --> 00:19:51,440
<i>♪ I'll follow wherever you go ♪</i>

331
00:19:51,523 --> 00:19:52,858
<i>♪ Oh, baby ♪</i>

332
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:56,987
<i>♪ I'll ride your wave ♪</i>

333
00:19:57,070 --> 00:20:00,699
<i>♪ Wherever it takes me ♪</i>

334
00:20:00,782 --> 00:20:05,787
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

335
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:08,707
<i>♪ Wherever I go ♪</i>

336
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:12,461
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

337
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:16,298
<i>♪ Even if you let go</i>
<i>I'll come back ♪</i>

338
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:18,091
<i>- ♪ Do you know ♪</i>
<i>- Hey.</i>

339
00:20:18,175 --> 00:20:20,761
<i>♪ When I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

340
00:20:20,844 --> 00:20:23,931
<i>You keep rewatching that.</i>
<i>You miss him, don't you?</i>

341
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:26,892
- [UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]
<i>- ♪ I'm coming home ♪</i>

342
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:29,228
- [CHUCKLES]
- [CROWD CHEERING ON VIDEO]

343
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:30,729
<i>But honestly?</i>

344
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:34,900
<i>I doubt he will forgive you.</i>

345
00:20:34,983 --> 00:20:39,071
- [UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [CROWD CHEERING ON VIDEO]

346
00:20:39,154 --> 00:20:40,530
<i>I'll still try.</i>

347
00:20:40,614 --> 00:20:42,157
<i>He's the only family I have left.</i>

348
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:45,369
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

349
00:20:45,452 --> 00:20:47,079
<i>That video went viral, right?</i>

350
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:51,250
<i>Okay. How about this?</i>

351
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:53,001
<i>Let's say</i>

352
00:20:54,127 --> 00:20:57,506
<i>that he wasn't famous</i>
<i>and hadn't achieved anything in life.</i>

353
00:20:57,589 --> 00:20:59,383
<i>That he didn't own a business.</i>

354
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,677
<i>Would you still approach him?</i>

355
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:05,055
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

356
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:06,014
<i>Yes.</i>

357
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:08,308
<i>Dad.</i>

358
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:10,602
<i>I'm sorry I put you through all that.</i>

359
00:21:10,686 --> 00:21:15,440
<i>I should be blamed for</i>
<i>what happened to your sister, not you.</i>

360
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:19,486
<i>Thank you for understanding.</i>

361
00:21:20,696 --> 00:21:22,739
<i>I should be the one thanking you.</i>

362
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:29,204
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]
